#
# RESEED (hand-harvest, local on fix/retirement, forward-only): the §16 arena sub-crumb B — the C-leg
# `load_u64`/`store_u64` emitters, the first hard prerequisite for the Teko-arena-over-mmap keystone (the arena
# core reads/writes its own state as words at raw mmap'd addresses; those loads/stores had a native-leg lowering
# but NO C-backend emitter, so the arena core could not compile on the C leg). What this harvest carries:
#   - **§16 arena crumb B (compiler — codegen)**: `emit_load_u64`/`emit_store_u64` (`codegen.tks`, beside
#     `emit_ptr_word`), dispatched by bare last segment `load_u64`/`store_u64` in the `teko::mem` block:
#     - `load_u64(addr: u64): u64`  → `((uint64_t)*(volatile uint64_t *)(uintptr_t)(<addr>))`
#     - `store_u64(addr: u64, v: u64): void` → `(*(volatile uint64_t *)(uintptr_t)(<addr>) = (uint64_t)(<v>))`
#     `volatile` for the same reason the syscall helpers clobber `"memory"`: the arena reads back words a sibling
#     store or an mmap just wrote, and the optimiser must not elide/reorder across the raw address it cannot
#     alias-analyze. The checker signatures (`scope.tks`) and the native lowering (`lir/lower.tks` → `LLoad`/
#     `LStore`) were ALREADY present; this crumb adds only the missing C-backend emitters.
#
# NOT INERT IN SOURCE, BUT NO BEHAVIORAL CORPUS DIVERGENCE. The compiler's own corpus (`src/`) has ZERO call
# sites of `load_u64`/`store_u64` (grep-verified: only signature/dispatch/doc-comment declarations, no
# invocations), so the new emitters never fire on the self-image; the emitted C differs from the previous seed
# only by the new codegen SOURCE (the `emit_load_u64`/`emit_store_u64` fn bodies, which naturally appear in the
# self-image as their own `cb(...)` string-literal payloads) plus the mechanical line/offset shifts it induces —
# a function-add reseed with zero behavioral divergence. The `arena_loadstore` fixture is the only invoker.
#
# NATIVE LEG — already lowered (`lir/lower.tks`); this crumb touches only the C leg. The C leg is the target.
#
# GATE: SELF-REPRODUCE.
#   - C-route chain: gen0 (cc, WITH `-pthread`, from the PREVIOUS bootstrap `1b61761d`) built the tree →
#     emitted teko.c `7bc8eac4` (tc1); tc1 -> gen1; gen1 built the tree → tc2 `7bc8eac4b925f069d341621086009b29
#     a881d8aadcd8f81130705dbe65c9794a`; tc2 -> gen2; gen2 built the tree → tc3 `7bc8eac4…`. tc1 == tc2 == tc3,
#     byte-identical (sha256 below). No ladder: the corpus invokes neither builtin, so gen0 and gen1 emit the
#     self-image identically at tc1.
#   - cc-route: cc -std=c2x -w -g -pthread -I src/runtime -I src/assert bootstrap/teko.c
#     src/runtime/teko_rt.c src/assert/assert.c -lm -> gen; TEKO_BACKEND=c gen . -o out --no-verify
#     --release -> out/teko.c; sha256(out/teko.c) == sha256(bootstrap/teko.c) == below.
#   - MEM_PARANOID: `TEKO_BACKEND=c TEKO_MEM_PARANOID=1 gen . -o out --no-verify --release` exits 0 (whole-tree,
#     clean through emit+cc). As with the prior syscall crumbs, a first capped run tripped the arena's own
#     "out of memory (str concat)" guard at the emit at the ~5.6 GB / 6 GB-cap boundary and a re-run completed
#     exit 0 — a cap-boundary memory-pressure artifact (Doc-1 territory), NOT a memory-correctness violation.
#   - Regression: `examples/regressions/arena_loadstore/` — mmaps a page, `store_u64(addr, 0x1122334455667788)`,
#     `load_u64(addr)` reads the sentinel back (round-trip match), munmaps; the built binary exits 0. Proves the
#     C-leg load/store emitters operate correctly on real mmap'd memory (crumb A + B together).
# The self-reported peak of the whole-tree build was ~5.6 GB (within the 6 GB cap; local ladder cc dropped
